WEBVTT

00:09.490 --> 00:12.370
So it would seem the tower 
has perfected it, then?

00:15.430 --> 00:18.110
The hope of this world.

00:19.950 --> 00:22.720
The Doomsday Clock must be mistaken.

00:24.190 --> 00:28.280
He's like... a twig that 
might snap at any moment.

00:30.220 --> 00:32.780
The Celestial Stairway has been sealed.

00:32.780 --> 00:34.730
That will provide us some respite.

00:35.620 --> 00:41.790
A short spell before the Celestial Host 
lays waste to this world.

00:41.790 --> 00:45.130
In that time, I will see to many wands.

00:45.960 --> 00:49.530
And you shall see to a lone sword.

00:52.710 --> 00:55.280
Are you truly certain 
about this, Mercedes?

00:55.280 --> 00:58.790
So stubborn. How many times 
do you intend to ask me that?

01:01.500 --> 01:04.790
All of this is part 
of the deal you brought me.

01:12.150 --> 01:14.260
This is our pact, Finn.

01:14.260 --> 01:17.500
You will, without fail, produce someone
who can use the fifth element.

01:19.810 --> 01:24.190
This time, you must find the key 
that will tune this world.

01:24.190 --> 01:25.250
Yes.

01:25.250 --> 01:27.940
The geas is binding. I swear it to you.

01:33.760 --> 01:35.940
To protect this world...

01:36.610 --> 01:39.150
I will find my way to the wand and sword.

01:49.570 --> 01:50.720
Now then...

01:51.680 --> 01:54.970
There've been lots of twists and turns, 
but I've made it this far.

01:55.670 --> 01:58.930
Will what begins now
be the musical we hoped for...

02:00.040 --> 02:02.480
or will it be a merciless tragedy?

02:03.510 --> 02:05.980
Perhaps it will be an exceptional comedy.

02:06.990 --> 02:08.370
Show me.

02:08.370 --> 02:12.680
Where will the pact I made 
with the esteemed witch lead us?

02:29.000 --> 02:33.720
Episode 16
And the Story Begins

03:47.370 --> 03:48.120
Just now, that...

03:48.120 --> 03:49.120
It can't be.

03:53.410 --> 03:56.630
What is happening?

04:01.090 --> 04:02.390
<i>This is...</i>

04:02.680 --> 04:06.680
<i>That light is vanquishing 
the monsters one after another.</i>

04:13.400 --> 04:14.840
Halcon!

04:23.660 --> 04:24.720
Sion!

04:37.420 --> 04:39.300
Run, Sion!

04:39.750 --> 04:41.850
I can't... run.

04:42.320 --> 04:43.550
I won't!

04:43.910 --> 04:47.430
If it were him, he'd never run away!

04:47.850 --> 04:48.930
That coward...

04:48.930 --> 04:51.690
who's braver than anyone!

04:51.960 --> 04:55.940
I can do this, too! 
I will not let him beat me!

04:57.920 --> 04:59.550
<i>You have it all wrong, Sion.</i>

05:00.450 --> 05:03.470
<i>I was jealous. I was bitter.</i>

05:04.250 --> 05:05.440
<i>I was desperate.</i>

05:06.460 --> 05:08.850
<i>I've been chasing all of you 
all this time.</i>

05:09.200 --> 05:11.040
<i>I'm just a pathetic wretch.</i>

05:12.710 --> 05:15.630
<i>Which is why, from now on...</i>

05:33.670 --> 05:36.220
<i>I will be like a lone sword!</i>

05:34.650 --> 05:36.730
<b>Mageblade: Wis</b>

05:48.500 --> 05:50.440
Will, is that you?

05:51.140 --> 05:52.360
The laggard?

05:52.810 --> 05:53.640
You...

06:08.310 --> 06:10.520
The Devander has reached Central Flos!

06:11.100 --> 06:12.770
Headmistress, we have to evacuate!

06:13.060 --> 06:14.270
Boil!

06:14.270 --> 06:16.270
Keridos Aqualuum!

06:24.870 --> 06:27.890
<i>We've managed to forestall
an incursion into the academy.</i>

06:27.890 --> 06:30.120
<i>But just what is going on here?</i>

06:30.390 --> 06:32.210
Headmistress! We must leave here at—

06:32.210 --> 06:33.120
You will wait!

06:39.190 --> 06:40.130
That's...

06:53.420 --> 06:54.650
Let's see who wins.

07:03.660 --> 07:05.650
Wh-What's all that noise?

07:05.650 --> 07:07.660
It's coming from the heart of the city.

07:08.370 --> 07:10.910
<i>Could it be... he's fighting?</i>

07:11.230 --> 07:12.410
<i>Will is...</i>

07:12.780 --> 07:14.160
<i>Up ahead of us...</i>

07:15.420 --> 07:16.790
Hey, Wignall!

07:17.380 --> 07:19.040
You too, Lihanna?!

07:19.330 --> 07:22.980
Blast it! Get a hold of yourselves!

07:22.980 --> 07:26.050
I've got no magical energy left!

07:28.090 --> 07:29.550
Mommy, hurry!

07:29.980 --> 07:31.310
<i>That sound...</i>

07:31.710 --> 07:33.340
<i>Serfort!</i>

07:33.340 --> 07:34.980
<i>Don't tell me that's you!</i>

07:35.560 --> 07:37.560
<i>You'd make a stand?</i>

07:38.710 --> 07:40.360
<i>Against that beast?</i>

07:44.980 --> 07:45.900
Oh?

07:47.080 --> 07:48.160
That's...

07:53.110 --> 07:54.160
Will.

07:59.440 --> 08:01.060
Ouch...

08:02.340 --> 08:03.080
Huh?

08:03.830 --> 08:04.920
That boy...

08:07.230 --> 08:09.310
<i>He's fighting on even footing?</i>

08:09.310 --> 08:11.330
<i>Against a foe that bested him before?</i>

08:12.920 --> 08:13.810
Ed!

08:14.300 --> 08:16.100
Serah! You're—

08:16.550 --> 08:18.590
Ow!

08:18.590 --> 08:20.350
Still alive, I see.

08:20.790 --> 08:23.410
As ever, your only forte
 is your rotten luck.

08:23.410 --> 08:24.610
Oh, stuff it!

08:26.470 --> 08:29.110
More importantly, what's going on?

08:29.110 --> 08:31.870
Just who is that boy anyway, Ed?

08:37.220 --> 08:38.660
Renaisse! Jorua!

08:38.660 --> 08:39.500
What's happening?

08:39.500 --> 08:41.420
They're so fast, I have no idea!

08:41.420 --> 08:43.300
But... he's holding his own!

08:44.100 --> 08:46.010
We have to get out there
 and provide support!

08:46.690 --> 08:47.970
Don't, Emma!

08:48.260 --> 08:48.970
Palm!

08:49.280 --> 08:52.010
Magic doesn't work on that monster.

08:52.540 --> 08:55.970
And if we hit him, 
we'll only be getting in his way.

08:58.020 --> 08:59.940
Palm said it.

08:59.940 --> 09:03.260
Magic like ours won't do any good.
 Besides...

09:03.670 --> 09:05.720
That's the no-talent, right?

09:05.720 --> 09:09.240
Up until now, we've looked down on him. 
We've made fun of him.

09:09.630 --> 09:12.990
After all this time, 
what can we possibly do for him?

09:18.150 --> 09:22.250
B-But... he saved all of us!

09:24.020 --> 09:26.500
<i>Even now, he's still fighting for us!</i>

09:26.500 --> 09:30.010
<i>I know it's self-serving of me, but...</i>

09:30.300 --> 09:32.790
<i>There has to be something I can do!</i>

09:34.510 --> 09:38.750
Go!

09:40.310 --> 09:42.640
Beat that thing!

09:43.010 --> 09:45.900
Laggard!

09:46.220 --> 09:47.900
I know you can do it!

09:48.180 --> 09:49.920
Will!

09:50.400 --> 09:52.460
You can do it!

09:53.440 --> 09:54.740
Don't let it best you, Will!

09:54.740 --> 09:56.190
Don't falter! Keep pushing!

09:56.190 --> 09:59.080
You've come this far, so make it happen!

09:59.080 --> 10:03.670
You can do it! Laggard! 
Go! Keep at it! Will!

10:03.670 --> 10:04.830
Julius...

10:05.350 --> 10:06.590
Sion...

10:08.180 --> 10:09.590
<i>You can do it!</i>

10:10.190 --> 10:12.710
<i>You can do it, Will!</i>

10:13.270 --> 10:14.610
Go!

10:14.610 --> 10:15.970
That's it!

10:15.970 --> 10:17.340
You've got this!

10:17.340 --> 10:18.300
Please!

10:18.300 --> 10:20.340
Now! Take that thing down!

10:20.340 --> 10:21.470
Keep pushing!

10:21.470 --> 10:22.980
Strike back!

10:24.950 --> 10:25.900
Ed!

10:26.180 --> 10:29.400
I'm not leaving this to someone 
who can't use magic!

10:32.750 --> 10:35.600
You really haven't changed one bit.

10:35.600 --> 10:38.410
But now's not the time for that, is it?

10:39.410 --> 10:43.410
This isn't when you protect your student. 
It's when you believe in him!

10:45.120 --> 10:46.500
Pummel that thing!

10:46.500 --> 10:47.880
Don't you dare falter!

10:47.880 --> 10:49.960
Mister!

10:49.960 --> 10:52.760
<i>Win! Win!</i>

10:51.460 --> 10:54.910
You can do it! Hold fast!

10:55.540 --> 10:57.050
<i>Rigarden is...</i>

10:57.050 --> 10:59.050
<i>The whole world of magic is...</i>

10:59.050 --> 11:02.090
<i>cheering on a no-talent 
who can't use magic?</i>

11:02.540 --> 11:03.850
<i>How can this be?</i>

11:11.550 --> 11:13.430
<i>I've been miserable for so long.</i>

11:15.570 --> 11:17.860
<i>It's hurt for so long.</i>

11:19.240 --> 11:20.370
<i>People have disdained me.</i>

11:20.890 --> 11:22.210
<i>They've made fun of me.</i>

11:22.870 --> 11:25.590
<i>There were times 
I hated this world right back.</i>

11:27.570 --> 11:28.700
<i>And yet...</i>

11:28.700 --> 11:30.040
<i>Somewhere in my heart...</i>

11:31.020 --> 11:32.840
<i>I wanted them to acknowledge me!</i>

11:33.670 --> 11:35.880
<i>That's what I've wanted all this time!</i>

11:35.880 --> 11:40.250
Go! You can do it! Beat that thing! 
Will! Don't let it beat you! Hold out!

11:40.250 --> 11:44.190
<i>Even if this is the only time
 they ever cheer for me...</i>

11:46.860 --> 11:50.550
<i>This world that has given me 
the courage to fight.</i>

11:51.150 --> 11:52.780
<i>And I want to protect...</i>

11:54.250 --> 11:56.190
<i>all of them!</i>

12:07.680 --> 12:08.920
Lady Elfaria?

12:13.250 --> 12:14.630
<b>Moria Silver Blade</b>

12:14.710 --> 12:18.050
<b><u>Moria Silver Blade</u>

A weapon forged by Donnan for Will, who cannot use magic.
It's made of Moria silver, a magic repelling metal that reacts strongly to magical energy.
Mages abhor dwarves, and this sharp dwarven blade serves as proof of an outlier—a warrior.</b>

12:19.760 --> 12:23.050
<b><u>Multos (Multi-Elemental Mages)</u>

In Rigarden, where "one person, one affinity" is established as the norm, 
this term refers to those who can use magic from more than one element.
Even among mages in general, Multos are extraordinarily uncommon.
Notable Multos include magical academy headmistress
 Caldron Anouve and Arbiter Clairie Serah among others.</b>

12:42.570 --> 12:44.080
Will's sword!

12:44.510 --> 12:47.830
<i>Will's sword couldn't
hold up to his strength!</i>

12:47.830 --> 12:49.160
<i>This is bad.</i>

12:49.160 --> 12:51.510
<i>Without a weapon, 
he'll be thrown off balance.</i>

12:59.510 --> 13:00.840
Lady Elfaria?

13:01.320 --> 13:02.840
Halt, Elfaria.

13:03.630 --> 13:06.360
We are not permitted to leave this place.

13:06.360 --> 13:08.180
I have no intention of leaving.

13:08.790 --> 13:12.300
I'm simply watching from the balcony.

13:14.470 --> 13:15.440
Hey.

13:19.840 --> 13:22.240
Oh, but...

13:23.200 --> 13:25.450
I'm afraid my hand slipped.

13:54.510 --> 13:56.230
Fully charged...

13:58.790 --> 14:00.600
Albis Wis!

14:01.800 --> 14:02.870
That's...

14:03.550 --> 14:05.740
It's like that time with the Grand Duke.

14:06.180 --> 14:09.340
Will's sword has the ability 
to take on others' spells.

14:09.340 --> 14:10.250
But...

14:10.500 --> 14:13.350
Hey! Magic doesn't work on that thing!

14:13.350 --> 14:14.000
Will!

14:14.270 --> 14:16.420
No matter how strong 
that spell might be...

14:18.900 --> 14:19.750
<i>I can tell.</i>

14:21.030 --> 14:22.510
<i>This power is...</i>

14:23.510 --> 14:24.870
<i>one that will never...</i>

14:26.230 --> 14:28.120
<i>ever stop!</i>

14:42.270 --> 14:43.280
It can't be!

14:44.400 --> 14:47.780
<i>He sliced through it? He just 
fundamentally ignored the mage slayer?</i>

14:50.470 --> 14:51.700
<i>Wis...</i>

14:53.650 --> 14:55.550
What was that?!

14:55.550 --> 14:56.790
What's happening?!

14:57.130 --> 15:01.110
What kind of logic is this?! 
How'd he get through a Sleime?!

15:01.110 --> 15:05.800
That snotty little brat! Just who is he?!

15:07.020 --> 15:08.300
For real?

15:10.810 --> 15:13.310
That guy's incredible!

15:13.750 --> 15:16.690
<i>That wasn't magical energy. 
That power was...</i>

15:16.940 --> 15:20.340
<i>The fifth element. 
It's written of in the Lore.</i>

15:20.340 --> 15:22.820
<i>The Primeval Key that began the world.</i>

15:24.740 --> 15:27.570
<i>So you've found it, have you, Finn?</i>

15:28.530 --> 15:30.330
<i>You made a vow to the Mage Queen.</i>

15:30.750 --> 15:32.830
<i>Wand and sword...</i>

15:58.040 --> 15:59.350
<i>He's too powerful.</i>

15:59.750 --> 16:02.600
<i>What merciless, overwhelming power.</i>

16:02.600 --> 16:03.610
<i>It's just like...</i>

16:04.320 --> 16:06.110
<i>Albis Vina.</i>

16:08.830 --> 16:12.320
<i>It's like she and Will 
are fighting together.</i>

16:14.860 --> 16:16.780
Headless!

16:19.500 --> 16:20.700
Gates?

16:20.700 --> 16:22.130
There's still more coming?

16:22.830 --> 16:25.380
What are we supposed to do
about all of those?!

16:33.740 --> 16:35.200
<i>It doesn't matter.</i>

16:35.890 --> 16:38.000
<i>With the two together...</i>

16:41.510 --> 16:42.890
Overload.

16:45.250 --> 16:47.050
Full Burst!

16:51.350 --> 16:55.140
El Glace Frosse, El Seven!

17:06.070 --> 17:09.220
Fruzel Cardeneia!

17:09.510 --> 17:09.590
<b>Fruzel Cardenia</b>

17:24.240 --> 17:25.610
Let's end this.

17:56.640 --> 17:57.890
Will!

18:04.430 --> 18:07.110
He did it! He did it!

18:07.110 --> 18:09.530
Kiki, Will's done it!

18:10.410 --> 18:11.900
That's what I'm talking about!

18:12.660 --> 18:14.410
Will...

18:17.670 --> 18:20.910
I knew it! You're one amazing lad!

18:21.440 --> 18:23.410
That's my part-timer for you.

18:28.550 --> 18:29.670
Will...

18:37.930 --> 18:41.440
Magnificent. You're better
 than I ever imagined.

18:41.440 --> 18:44.700
You, the hope left to us here at the end.

18:47.890 --> 18:49.620
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mercedes!

18:50.180 --> 18:52.370
It's time for me to make good on our pact!

18:53.080 --> 18:56.100
What? It only took five hundred years.

18:56.100 --> 18:58.070
The slightest of miscalculations.

18:58.630 --> 19:01.500
Our long prologue ends here.

19:01.500 --> 19:04.130
Just you wait, false sky!

19:04.130 --> 19:05.580
The curtain is rising.

19:06.520 --> 19:08.340
Now, let us begin!

19:08.340 --> 19:12.090
A tale of the joining of wand and sword! 
The story of all of you—Wistoria!

23:28.970 --> 23:31.060
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

23:36.230 --> 23:38.600
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword,</i>

23:38.980 --> 23:41.870
episode 17, "The Day of Departure."

23:40.520 --> 23:46.030
Episode 17
The Day of Departure
